from (values
('127.404.d.7.D',3,'A frayed power cord is dangerous because it can cause:','["music", "clean air", "cooling", "shock or fire"]'::jsonb,3,'Damaged insulation exposes wires.','original'),
('127.404.d.7.D',4,'Overloading an extension cord with many tools can lead to:','["overheating and fire", "faster work", "better power", "cooler wires"]'::jsonb,0,'Excess current heats the cord.','original'),
('127.404.d.7.E',3,'Double-insulated tools and GFCI outlets are ways to:','["increase noise", "reduce the risk of electric shock", "save paint", "add weight"]'::jsonb,1,'Controls prevent shock.','original'),
('127.404.d.7.E',4,'Before repairing a machine, a technician should disconnect the power and apply:','["a warning song", "a sticker for decoration", "a lockout device", "a coat of paint"]'::jsonb,2,'Lockout prevents startup.','original'),
('127.404.d.7.F',3,'An eyewash station is a workplace resource used for:','["cooling drinks", "storing tools", "washing cars", "flushing chemicals from the eyes"]'::jsonb,3,'Eyewash stations are emergency equipment.','original'),
('127.404.d.7.F',4,'An emergency evacuation map in a lab shows exits and:','["assembly areas", "menu items", "sale prices", "team scores"]'::jsonb,0,'Maps guide people to safety.','original'),
('127.404.d.7.G',3,'Used oil rags that can ignite should be placed in:','["the sink", "an approved metal container with a lid", "an open bin", "a paper bag"]'::jsonb,1,'Oily rags can self-heat.','original'),
('127.404.d.7.G',4,'Hazardous waste containers should be labeled with their:','["color", "owner''s pet", "contents", "price"]'::jsonb,2,'Labels identify hazards.','original'),
('127.404.d.7.H',3,'Routine maintenance of a drill press includes checking the:','["poster", "wallpaper", "lunch box", "belt and lubrication"]'::jsonb,3,'Regular checks prevent breakdowns.','original'),
('127.404.d.7.H',4,'Dull cutting tools should be:','["sharpened or replaced", "used harder", "painted", "hidden"]'::jsonb,0,'Sharp tools are safer.','original'),
('127.404.d.7.I',3,'After use, hand tools should be:','["left on the floor", "cleaned and returned to storage", "lent without asking", "thrown in a bin"]'::jsonb,1,'Proper storage prevents loss and damage.','original'),
('127.404.d.7.J',3,'Using a damaged ladder can result in:','["savings", "faster work", "serious injury", "a promotion"]'::jsonb,2,'Defective equipment injures workers.','original'),
('127.404.d.7.J',4,'A company may face lawsuits and fines if equipment maintenance is:','["documented", "scheduled", "inspected", "neglected"]'::jsonb,3,'Negligence has consequences.','original'),
('127.404.d.3.A',4,'An engineering notebook is treated as legal evidence in part because its pages are:','["bound, numbered, and signed", "pencil-only", "loose and undated", "shared with competitors"]'::jsonb,0,'Bound, signed pages resist tampering.','original'),
('127.404.d.8.A',3,'A square scaled up by a factor of 2 has sides that are:','["the same", "twice as long", "half as long", "four times as long"]'::jsonb,1,'Linear scale factor multiplies lengths.','original'),
('127.404.d.8.A',4,'If a square''s sides are doubled, its area becomes:','["two times larger", "the same", "four times larger", "half as large"]'::jsonb,2,'Area scales with the square of the factor.','original'),
('127.404.d.8.B',3,'To draw a cube in three dimensions, a drafter must define length, width, and:','["color", "price", "weight", "height"]'::jsonb,3,'3D needs a third dimension.','original'),
('127.404.d.8.B',4,'An isometric drawing shows the three principal axes separated by:','["120 degrees", "90 degrees only", "45 degrees", "30 degrees total"]'::jsonb,0,'Isometric axes are 120 degrees apart.','original'),
('127.404.d.8.C',3,'The front, top, and right-side views of an object are called its:','["animations", "2D views", "3D renders", "samples"]'::jsonb,1,'Views flatten a 3D object into 2D.','original'),
('127.404.d.8.C',4,'In a third-angle projection, the top view is placed:','["to the left of the front view", "on another sheet", "above the front view", "below the front view"]'::jsonb,2,'U.S. standard places the top view above.','original'),
('127.404.d.8.D',3,'A figure has symmetry if one half is a mirror image of the:','["scale", "label", "background", "other half"]'::jsonb,3,'Mirror symmetry matches halves.','original'),
('127.404.d.8.D',4,'Scaling a triangle by a factor of 3 and keeping its angles the same produces a figure that is:','["similar to the original", "smaller", "unrelated", "congruent"]'::jsonb,0,'Proportional scaling preserves shape.','original'),
('127.404.d.9.A',3,'A drawing that shows the front, top, and side of a part is a:','["mind map", "multi-view projection", "rendering", "cartoon"]'::jsonb,1,'Multi-view uses several views.','original'),
('127.404.d.9.A',4,'A single-view drawing is sufficient only when the object is:','["an engine", "very complex", "simple, such as a flat part with a note about its thickness", "a full assembly"]'::jsonb,2,'Flat parts can use one view.','original'),
('127.404.d.9.B',3,'In a technical drawing, hidden edges are shown with:','["thick solid lines", "dimension lines", "wavy lines", "dashed lines"]'::jsonb,3,'Hidden lines are dashed.','original'),
('127.404.d.9.B',4,'A thin line made of long and short dashes alternating marks the:','["center of a circle or symmetrical part", "cutting plane only", "outline of the part", "hidden surface"]'::jsonb,0,'Center lines show axes.','original'),
('127.404.d.9.C',3,'An orthographic view shows an object straight on, while a pictorial view shows it:','["as a list", "as it appears in three dimensions", "without depth", "as a table"]'::jsonb,1,'Pictorials show depth.','original'),
('127.404.d.9.C',4,'A perspective drawing differs from an isometric drawing because in perspective, parallel lines:','["never meet", "become dashed", "appear to converge toward vanishing points", "become thick"]'::jsonb,2,'Perspective mimics vision.','original'),
('127.404.d.9.D',3,'An auxiliary view is used to show the true shape of a surface that is:','["parallel to the front", "hidden", "horizontal", "inclined to the normal views"]'::jsonb,3,'Slanted faces appear distorted in standard views.','original'),
('127.404.d.9.D',4,'To create an auxiliary view, projection lines are drawn perpendicular to the:','["inclined surface", "horizontal line", "page edge", "title block"]'::jsonb,0,'Auxiliary projection is perpendicular to the slanted face.','original'),
('127.404.d.9.E',3,'A section view is created by imagining a:','["reflection", "cutting plane passing through the object", "shadow", "paint layer"]'::jsonb,1,'Sections reveal interior detail.','original'),
('127.404.d.9.E',4,'The thin angled lines in a section view show the:','["dimensions", "hidden holes", "surface that was cut", "center lines"]'::jsonb,2,'Section lines mark cut surfaces.','original'),
('127.404.d.9.F',3,'A production drawing must include dimensions, tolerances, and:','["fancy colors", "advertising", "jokes", "notes and material callouts"]'::jsonb,3,'Production drawings guide manufacturing.','original'),
('127.404.d.9.F',4,'When a design changes, the drawing must be revised and the revision recorded in the:','["revision block", "file name only", "email subject", "page margin"]'::jsonb,0,'Revision blocks track changes.','original'),
('127.404.d.9.G',3,'Naming CADD files with a clear system helps team members to:','["hide drawings", "find the right file quickly", "lose files", "overwrite work"]'::jsonb,1,'File structure supports teamwork.','original'),
('127.404.d.9.G',4,'Keeping a backup copy of drawing files protects against:','["better lighting", "email", "accidental loss", "paper jams"]'::jsonb,2,'Backups prevent data loss.','original'),
('127.404.d.9.H',3,'Annotation scale in CADD lets text and dimensions:','["change colors", "print blank", "disappear", "display at a consistent size in different viewports"]'::jsonb,3,'Annotative objects adjust to scale.','original'),
('127.404.d.9.H',4,'A tolerance of ±0.005 inch on a shaft diameter tells the machinist how much the size may:','["vary from the nominal value", "change in price", "change in color", "change in label"]'::jsonb,0,'Tolerance sets acceptable variation.','original'),
('127.404.d.9.I',3,'A 3D CADD model can be used to make a prototype with a:','["pencil", "3D printer", "fax machine", "stapler"]'::jsonb,1,'CAD models feed additive manufacturing.','original'),
('127.404.d.9.I',4,'An STL file is commonly used to send a CADD model to a:','["spreadsheet", "speaker", "3D printer", "camera"]'::jsonb,2,'STL describes surface geometry for printing.','original'),
('127.404.d.10.A',3,'Computer-aided design (CAD) lets designers create parts using:','["only clay", "only paper", "only wood", "digital tools"]'::jsonb,3,'CAD uses software.','original'),
('127.404.d.10.A',4,'Designing a part with simulation of loads before building helps an engineer to:','["predict failure points", "reduce thinking", "avoid math", "skip testing forever"]'::jsonb,0,'Simulation finds weak areas.','original'),
('127.404.d.10.B',3,'Different CADD programs are chosen based on the:','["weather", "type of design work", "calendar", "lunch"]'::jsonb,1,'Mechanical and architectural programs differ.','original'),
('127.404.d.10.B',4,'Parametric modeling software is most helpful for designs that:','["are drawn once", "have no dimensions", "change often and need related updates", "never change"]'::jsonb,2,'Parametric models update with parameters.','original'),
('127.404.d.10.C',3,'An engineering drawing follows standards so that anyone reading it:','["guesses the meaning", "ignores it", "can change it freely", "interprets it the same way"]'::jsonb,3,'Standards make drawings universal.','original'),
('127.404.d.10.C',4,'ASME Y14.5 is a standard for:','["dimensioning and tolerancing", "music", "cooking", "painting"]'::jsonb,0,'Y14.5 governs GD&T.','original'),
('127.404.d.10.D',3,'Reliability in design means the product will:','["cost less", "perform correctly for its expected life", "fail soon", "look pretty"]'::jsonb,1,'Reliability is consistent performance.','original'),
('127.404.d.10.D',4,'Adding a guard over a rotating shaft is an example of designing in:','["price", "weight", "safety", "color"]'::jsonb,2,'Guards prevent injury.','original'),
('127.404.d.10.E',3,'A designer who adds large buttons to a device for users with limited dexterity is addressing:','["fashion", "branding", "pricing", "special needs"]'::jsonb,3,'Inclusive design helps everyone.','original'),
('127.404.d.10.E',4,'Universal design aims to make products usable by:','["as many people as possible", "one age group", "engineers only", "experts only"]'::jsonb,0,'Universal design widens access.','original'),
('127.404.d.10.F',3,'A patent gives an inventor the right to stop others from making or selling the invention for a limited:','["color", "time", "place name", "size"]'::jsonb,1,'Patents expire.','original'),
('127.404.d.10.F',4,'Before filing a patent, an inventor should search existing patents to see if the idea is:','["too cheap", "too quiet", "already protected", "too colorful"]'::jsonb,2,'Prior art searches avoid duplication.','original'),
