('127.404.d.11.A',4,'Listing the order of assembly steps before building a prototype helps avoid:','["testing", "measurements", "mistakes and wasted materials", "feedback"]'::jsonb,2,'Sequences save materials.','original'),
('127.404.d.11.B',3,'A band saw is used mainly to:','["weld", "measure", "paint", "cut shapes from sheet material"]'::jsonb,3,'Band saws cut curves.','original'),
('127.404.d.11.B',4,'Selecting a material that is strong but lightweight for a drone frame shows consideration of:','["material properties", "color only", "slogan", "name"]'::jsonb,0,'Properties guide choices.','original'),
('127.404.d.11.C',3,'When presenting a prototype, a team should explain how it meets the:','["weather", "project requirements", "school calendar", "fashion trends"]'::jsonb,1,'Connect results to requirements.','original'),
('127.404.d.11.C',4,'A demonstration of a prototype is stronger when the team also shares:','["opinions only", "jokes", "test data supporting claims", "lunch plans"]'::jsonb,2,'Evidence builds credibility.','original'),
('127.404.d.11.D',3,'A prototype that holds 20 kg when the requirement was 15 kg is a:','["flaw", "mistake", "failure", "success for that criterion"]'::jsonb,3,'Exceeding the requirement is a pass.','original'),
('127.404.d.11.D',4,'Evaluating a prototype in context means judging it against the original:','["problem and requirements", "price tags", "names", "colors"]'::jsonb,0,'Context is the design brief.','original'),
('127.404.d.12.A',3,'Defining an engineering problem begins with describing the:','["logo", "need or gap", "answer", "price"]'::jsonb,1,'Problems begin with needs.','original'),
('127.404.d.12.A',4,'A problem definition that names the user, the need, and a measurable goal is:','["vague", "personal", "specific and testable", "complete without data"]'::jsonb,2,'Strong definitions are measurable.','original'),
('127.404.d.12.B',3,'Goals, objectives, and requirements describe what the solution:','["is named", "looks like only", "will cost in lunch", "must accomplish"]'::jsonb,3,'Requirements define success.','original'),
('127.404.d.12.B',4,'An objective for a water filter might be to remove at least 99 percent of:','["particles from water", "light from rooms", "colors from paper", "sound from air"]'::jsonb,0,'Objectives are measurable targets.','original'),
('127.404.d.12.C',3,'Choosing a material for a product requires comparing strength, cost, and:','["color of the cover", "availability", "brand slogan", "weather"]'::jsonb,1,'Properties and supply matter.','original'),
('127.404.d.12.C',4,'A material that resists rust is important for a product used:','["in a vacuum", "only at night", "outdoors in wet conditions", "indoors in a dry drawer"]'::jsonb,2,'Corrosion resistance matters outdoors.','original'),
('127.404.d.12.D',3,'Manufacturability means a design can be:','["imagined", "painted", "hidden", "produced efficiently and consistently"]'::jsonb,3,'Designs must be buildable.','original'),
('127.404.d.12.D',4,'Maintainability matters in a design because parts that wear out should be:','["easy to replace", "glued permanently", "sealed forever", "impossible to reach"]'::jsonb,0,'Serviceable designs last longer.','original'),
('127.404.d.12.E',3,'A limited budget is a design constraint on:','["color names", "funding", "gravity", "time zones"]'::jsonb,1,'Funding limits choices.','original'),
('127.404.d.12.E',4,'Determining that only two people can work on a project is a constraint on:','["materials", "brand", "personnel", "weather"]'::jsonb,2,'People are a resource.','original'),
('127.404.d.12.F',3,'Requirements for a new playground include health, safety, and:','["clothing styles", "favorite songs", "sports teams", "environmental concerns"]'::jsonb,3,'Social and environmental impacts matter.','original'),
('127.404.d.12.F',4,'Choosing recyclable materials addresses which type of requirement?','["environmental", "financial only", "legal only", "musical"]'::jsonb,0,'Recycling reduces waste.','original'),
('127.404.d.12.G',3,'A team that lists several different ways to solve a problem is finding:','["errors", "alternative solutions", "one answer", "excuses"]'::jsonb,1,'Alternatives expand options.','original'),
('127.404.d.12.G',4,'Drawing a morphological chart lets a team combine:','["colors only", "random facts", "options for each function to form solutions", "budgets only"]'::jsonb,2,'It builds concepts from options.','original'),
('127.404.d.12.H',3,'Testing proposed solutions with a simple model or simulation helps a team to:','["ignore data", "hide results", "avoid choosing", "compare how well they work"]'::jsonb,3,'Tests reveal differences.','original'),
('127.404.d.12.H',4,'Failure mode and effects analysis helps engineers to:','["identify risks and rank them by severity", "write songs", "pick colors", "reduce meetings"]'::jsonb,0,'FMEA prioritizes risks.','original'),
