('127.405.d.2.A',4,'A design process diagram often shows arrows going back to earlier steps because designs are:','["refined through repeated testing", "random", "finished in a day", "done once"]'::jsonb,0,'Iteration is expected.','original'),
('127.405.d.2.B',3,'Adding more features to a product increases its:','["silence", "complexity", "color", "simplicity"]'::jsonb,1,'More features mean more complexity.','original'),
('127.405.d.2.B',4,'A project with an unclear scope often suffers because the team cannot agree on what is:','["the team name", "on the lunch menu", "included in the work", "the team color"]'::jsonb,2,'Scope sets limits.','original'),
('127.405.d.2.C',3,'A customer, a neighbor, and an inspector are all parties with an:','["no role", "identical goals", "equal budget", "interest in the design"]'::jsonb,3,'Interested parties influence design.','original'),
('127.405.d.2.C',4,'An environmental group asking for less pollution from a factory shows how parties can:','["change design requirements", "end the project", "build the product", "remove tests"]'::jsonb,0,'Outside groups shape constraints.','original'),
('127.405.d.2.D',3,'An engineer who treats a failed test as a chance to learn is showing:','["anger", "a growth approach to design", "laziness", "carelessness"]'::jsonb,1,'Failure informs improvement.','original'),
('127.405.d.2.D',4,'Studying a collapsed roof to understand why it failed is called:','["stock trading", "cosmetics", "forensic engineering", "marketing"]'::jsonb,2,'Forensic engineering investigates failures.','original'),
('127.405.d.3.A',3,'The planning phase of a project produces a:','["final product", "trophy", "new logo", "schedule, budget, and scope plan"]'::jsonb,3,'Planning defines the work.','original'),
('127.405.d.3.A',4,'In which phase does the team actually build the deliverables?','["execution", "initiation", "closing", "planning"]'::jsonb,0,'Execution does the work.','original'),
('127.405.d.3.B',3,'A team member on an engineering project is expected to complete assigned tasks and:','["hide issues", "communicate problems early", "avoid meetings", "work alone only"]'::jsonb,1,'Early communication prevents delays.','original'),
('127.405.d.3.B',4,'Which role approves major changes and resolves conflicts on a project?','["visitor", "intern", "project manager or sponsor", "supplier''s driver"]'::jsonb,2,'Leaders decide.','original'),
