('127.405.d.8.G',4,'Standard fittings such as bolts and nuts are placed in a drawing from a:','["parts library", "calendar", "sketch pad", "spreadsheet"]'::jsonb,0,'Libraries hold standard parts.','original'),
('127.405.d.8.H',3,'An annotation style controls how text, dimensions, and leaders:','["sound", "look on the drawing", "move files", "cost"]'::jsonb,1,'Styles standardize appearance.','original'),
('127.405.d.8.H',4,'Setting a dimension style that uses decimal inches to three places gives dimensions like:','["1 1/4", "1.25 or about 1", "1.250", "5/4"]'::jsonb,2,'Three decimal places show 1.250.','original'),
('127.405.d.8.I',3,'A layout (paper space) can hold multiple viewports at different:','["owners", "names", "colors", "scales"]'::jsonb,3,'Viewports can scale independently.','original'),
('127.405.d.8.I',4,'An advanced layout technique places a detail view at 2:1 next to a main view at 1:4 to show:','["a small feature clearly", "more files", "more layers", "a new color"]'::jsonb,0,'Detail views magnify small features.','original'),
('127.405.d.8.J',3,'Layers let a drafter control which parts of a drawing are:','["owned", "visible and printed", "solved", "spelled"]'::jsonb,1,'Layers organize visibility.','original'),
('127.405.d.8.J',4,'Freezing a layer differs from turning it off because a frozen layer is also ignored during:','["saving files", "naming layers", "regeneration", "printing paper"]'::jsonb,2,'Freezing speeds up regen.','original'),
('127.405.d.8.K',3,'A custom template stores a company''s title block and:','["old projects", "pictures", "passwords", "standard settings"]'::jsonb,3,'Templates save setup time.','original'),
('127.405.d.8.K',4,'An advanced template may include layer standards, text styles, and:','["plot settings", "song lists", "recipes", "passwords"]'::jsonb,0,'Templates package standards.','original'),
('127.405.d.8.L',3,'Polar tracking helps a drafter draw lines at set:','["prices", "angles", "colors", "names"]'::jsonb,1,'Polar tracking snaps to angles.','original'),
('127.405.d.8.L',4,'Blocks saved with attributes let a drafter insert symbols that also carry:','["music", "video", "text information", "coins"]'::jsonb,2,'Attributes hold data.','original'),
('127.405.d.8.M',3,'An external reference (xref) shows another drawing without:','["using layers", "having scale", "having a name", "copying its geometry into the file"]'::jsonb,3,'Xrefs link instead of copy.','original'),
('127.405.d.8.M',4,'When the source file of an xref changes, the main drawing can:','["reload to show the update", "delete itself", "change name", "lose its layers"]'::jsonb,0,'Xrefs update.','original'),
('127.405.d.8.N',3,'Parametric modeling tools allow the model to change when a:','["tab is closed", "dimension value is edited", "color is picked", "file is renamed"]'::jsonb,1,'Parameters drive geometry.','original'),
('127.405.d.8.N',4,'Rendering a model adds realistic materials and lighting so viewers can:','["weigh it", "measure it", "judge its appearance before it is built", "cut it"]'::jsonb,2,'Renders visualize designs.','original'),
('127.405.d.8.O',3,'An animated assembly shows how parts:','["are named", "are stored", "are priced", "move and fit together"]'::jsonb,3,'Animation shows motion.','original'),
('127.405.d.8.O',4,'A motion study in an assembly model can reveal whether two moving parts will:','["collide", "save", "rename", "print"]'::jsonb,0,'Interference checks find collisions.','original'),
('127.405.d.9.A',3,'Delineating the steps of the design process for a prototype begins with defining the problem and generating:','["press releases", "possible solutions", "finished goods", "invoices"]'::jsonb,1,'Design starts with problem and ideas.','original'),
('127.405.d.9.A',4,'Implementing the plan after choosing a solution means:','["hiding the plan", "ending the project", "building and testing the prototype", "buying a bigger budget"]'::jsonb,2,'Implementation follows planning.','original'),
('127.405.d.9.B',3,'Before using a drill press, a student should secure the workpiece with a:','["bare hand", "friend''s hand", "glove", "clamp or vise"]'::jsonb,3,'Clamp the work.','original'),
('127.405.d.9.B',4,'When using a machine with rotating parts, loose sleeves and jewelry should be:','["removed or secured", "left on", "ignored", "tightened loosely"]'::jsonb,0,'Loose items entangle.','original'),
('127.405.d.9.C',3,'A material for a prototype should be chosen based on its:','["name only", "properties and cost", "brand only", "color only"]'::jsonb,1,'Properties and cost guide choices.','original'),
('127.405.d.9.C',4,'Prototype material and production material may differ because prototypes often use:','["gold", "unavailable materials", "cheaper, easier-to-work materials", "dangerous chemicals"]'::jsonb,2,'Prototypes use convenient materials.','original'),
('127.405.d.9.D',3,'Usability in design means a product is easy to:','["hide", "break", "sell only", "learn and use"]'::jsonb,3,'Usability matters.','original'),
('127.405.d.9.D',4,'A product with high performance, usability, and reliability is said to have good:','["design quality", "paint", "packaging only", "advertising"]'::jsonb,0,'Quality has several dimensions.','original'),
('127.405.d.9.E',3,'Quality-control requirements for a part may include checking its:','["color of the box", "dimensions against the drawing", "name tag", "lunch"]'::jsonb,1,'Inspections verify specs.','original'),
('127.405.d.9.E',4,'A go/no-go gauge is a quality tool used to check whether a part is:','["heavy", "painted", "within tolerance", "hot"]'::jsonb,2,'Gauges test limits quickly.','original'),
('127.405.d.9.F',3,'Evaluating prototype quality means comparing results to the design:','["fonts", "slogans", "decorations", "criteria"]'::jsonb,3,'Criteria define success.','original'),
('127.405.d.9.F',4,'A prototype that meets size and weight but fails the strength test has:','["met some criteria but not all", "met none", "an unknown design", "met all criteria"]'::jsonb,0,'Evaluate each criterion.','original'),
('127.405.d.9.G',3,'A systems engineering approach treats a prototype as a set of:','["colors", "connected subsystems", "stickers", "unrelated parts"]'::jsonb,1,'Systems thinking links parts.','original'),
('127.405.d.9.G',4,'Testing each subsystem before assembling the whole prototype helps to:','["delay testing", "hide problems", "find problems early", "avoid documentation"]'::jsonb,2,'Subsystem testing isolates faults.','original'),
('127.405.d.9.H',3,'A prototype presentation should show how the design meets each:','["snack", "joke", "slogan", "requirement"]'::jsonb,3,'Link design to requirements.','original'),
('127.405.d.9.H',4,'The strongest evidence in a prototype presentation is:','["measured test results", "guesses", "opinions", "advertising"]'::jsonb,0,'Data is credible.','original'),
('127.405.d.10.A',3,'A multi-system problem might involve mechanical, electrical, and:','["sports gear", "software systems", "cooking tools", "art supplies"]'::jsonb,1,'Complex products combine systems.','original'),
('127.405.d.10.A',4,'A robotic vacuum is a multi-system product because it combines motors, sensors, and a:','["plug-in clock only", "rug", "control program", "nap"]'::jsonb,2,'It integrates hardware and software.','original'),
('127.405.d.10.B',3,'Documenting goals and requirements for a complex project makes sure all team members:','["argue", "avoid work", "hide tasks", "share the same expectations"]'::jsonb,3,'Documented requirements align teams.','original'),
('127.405.d.10.B',4,'A requirement is testable when it includes a:','["measurable value", "slogan", "color name", "feeling"]'::jsonb,0,'Testable requirements are measurable.','original'),
('127.405.d.10.C',3,'Design constraints on a project can include materials, personnel, and:','["moods", "time", "slogans", "songs"]'::jsonb,1,'Time is a constraint.','original'),
('127.405.d.10.C',4,'A limit on available motors forces a team to select a design that works with the:','["wishes", "imagination only", "parts on hand", "unlimited catalog"]'::jsonb,2,'Constraints guide selection.','original'),
('127.405.d.10.D',3,'Health, safety, and environmental concerns are examples of design:','["nicknames", "themes", "rumors", "parameters"]'::jsonb,3,'They shape design.','original'),
('127.405.d.10.D',4,'Social requirements may include accessibility for people with:','["different abilities", "no abilities", "identical abilities", "no needs"]'::jsonb,0,'Accessible design is a social requirement.','original'),
('127.405.d.10.E',3,'Creating several possible solutions for a complex system problem helps the team to:','["avoid choices", "compare options", "hide data", "skip testing"]'::jsonb,1,'Alternatives enable comparison.','original'),
('127.405.d.10.E',4,'Combining a motor from one idea with a sensor from another to make a new concept is called:','["repetition", "subtraction", "synthesis of alternatives", "erasure"]'::jsonb,2,'Concept synthesis builds new solutions.','original'),
('127.405.d.10.F',3,'Tools such as simulation or a test rig help a team to:','["hide errors", "avoid testing", "sell products", "evaluate a proposed solution"]'::jsonb,3,'Tools support evaluation.','original'),
('127.405.d.10.F',4,'Running a computer simulation before building a multi-system product can reveal:','["design problems early", "a team name", "a marketing plan", "a lunch menu"]'::jsonb,0,'Early detection saves cost.','original'),
('127.405.d.10.G',3,'A justified solution is supported by data and the:','["logo color", "requirements it meets", "team''s mascot", "weather"]'::jsonb,1,'Justification cites requirements.','original'),
('127.405.d.10.G',4,'Selecting the preferred multi-system solution using a weighted matrix shows the use of:','["favoritism", "luck", "structured decision-making", "guessing"]'::jsonb,2,'Structure reduces bias.','original')
